# Version bump + build required
After ANY code change: python update-version.py bugfix (or minor), then npm run build. Chrome loads from dist/.

# Avoid opening or activating tabs
Avoid opening or activating tabs whenever possible; prefer background fetch / offscreen / content scripts in user-opened pages. Don't change URLs of user tabs. If unavoidable: inactive tab, closed when done, via withBackgroundTab (lib/tab-scraper-utils.js). See AGENTS.md and harness/invariants.md (I1).

# Git repo + mandatory commit/tag each release
Verify at start: git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree (expect true).

After version bump + build (each release):
1) Read version from chrome-extension/manifest.json "version"
2) git add -A
3) git commit (e.g. chore: release X.Y.Z)
4) git tag -a X.Y.Z -m "X.Y.Z" — tag = manifest version, no v prefix

Only commit/tag if there are changes. Never push unless the user explicitly asks.
